Source: the --grab-delay-ms argument of the CI-only probe scripts/ci/xres-owner.c, parsed by strtol and refused only when negative, out of long range or followed by text (scripts/ci/xres-owner.c:864-867); there is no upper bound. Sink: delay_ms + 999 in the alarm that bounds the server-grab bracket (scripts/ci/xres-owner.c:975), armed just before XGrabServer. Above LONG_MAX-999 it overflows (undefined behaviour); a value such as 4294967291000 wraps to alarm(0), so the grab plus sleep_ms(delay_ms) would be unbounded. Not exploitable as shipped: the workflows pass only --mode wm --owner-pid (.github/workflows/release.yml:614), so delay_ms is 0 and the bound is 5 s; scripts/ is not published. Verdict hardening: refuse delay_ms above a small ceiling in the same check. Not required before publication.
